    "temperature": {
      "file": "oxalate_removal_system_temperature.glb",
      "title": "Why oxalate must be removed",
      "description": "Organic matter in bauxite degrades in the hot caustic liquor to sodium oxalate. If it builds up, oxalate co-precipitates with gibbsite, giving fine, weak hydrate and lower yield. A side-stream is cooled and seeded with oxalate crystals so oxalate crystallises in a controlled way; crystals are separated (cyclones/filters) and destroyed (e.g. by lime or burning), and the clean liquor returns.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
